-- An imported contract that reads a section GIVEN, named as an operand of RAND
-- or ROR (smucclaw/l4-ide#1118).
--
-- `pay leg` comes from ok/section-given-import-contract-def.l4, where `dl` is 5
-- by default, so Alice has until 5 to pay. Named here, it is a closure that has
-- to be applied to that module's own cell before it is a contract. Evaluating
-- it on its own, or as a HENCE or a LEST, always did that. As an operand of
-- RAND or ROR it did not: the compound applies its operand to the time and the
-- events, and those two arguments reached the closure in place of the cell. A
-- reader of one section GIVEN then stopped with "given signatures' values'
-- lengths do not match" (evaluations 1 to 26), and a reader of two took the
-- time and the events for its two inputs and went on, giving a wrong answer
-- with no error (27 and 28, `two section GIVENs`). The same happened when the
-- reader sat under an IF, a CONSIDER, a WHERE or a LET that was itself the
-- operand. Parentheses change nothing: the parser keeps no node for them.
--
-- Evaluations 1 to 28 are the fourteen operand shapes, each run twice: Alice
-- pays at 4 (in time) and at 7 (late), and Bob never acts. Evaluations 29 to 39
-- are the cases that already worked, and must go on working (the last two have
-- a compound inside a HENCE, where the operand was applied already). In a
-- single file, with the section GIVEN beside the rule, every evaluation gives
-- the answer it gives here; the CLI test that runs this file compares the two.

IMPORT `section-given-import-contract-def`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`left reader` MEANS
    `pay leg` RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`right reader` MEANS
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10) RAND `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`or, left reader` MEANS
    `pay leg` ROR (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`or, right reader` MEANS
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10) ROR `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`both readers` MEANS
    `pay leg` RAND `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`or, both readers` MEANS
    `pay leg` ROR `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`nested left` MEANS
    (`pay leg` RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 12)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`nested right` MEANS
    (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 12) RAND ((PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10) ROR `pay leg`)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`under an IF, then` MEANS
    (IF TRUE THEN `pay leg` ELSE FULFILLED) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`under an IF, else` MEANS
    (IF FALSE THEN FULFILLED ELSE `pay leg`) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`under a CONSIDER` MEANS
    (CONSIDER TRUE
     WHEN TRUE THEN `pay leg`
     WHEN FALSE THEN FULFILLED) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`under a WHERE` MEANS
    (`pay leg` WHERE `unused` MEANS 1) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`under a LET` MEANS
    (LET `unused` MEANS 1 IN `pay leg`) RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`two section GIVENs` MEANS
    `pay then deliver` RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`plain reader` MEANS
    `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`no section GIVEN` MEANS
    `plain leg` RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10)

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`as a HENCE` MEANS
    PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE `pay leg` LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "late"

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`as a LEST, met` MEANS
    PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`as a LEST, missed` MEANS
    PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10 HENCE FULFILLED LEST `pay leg`

GIVETH A DEONTIC Person Action
`in a HENCE` MEANS
    PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 10
    HENCE (`pay leg` RAND (PARTY Bob MUST deliver WITHIN 5))
    LEST BREACH BY Bob BECAUSE "late"

#TRACE `left reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `left reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `right reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `right reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `or, left reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `or, left reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `or, right reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `or, right reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `both readers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `both readers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `or, both readers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `or, both readers` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `nested left` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `nested left` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `nested right` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `nested right` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under an IF, then` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under an IF, then` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under an IF, else` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under an IF, else` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under a CONSIDER` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under a CONSIDER` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under a WHERE` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under a WHERE` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under a LET` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `under a LET` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `two section GIVENs` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `two section GIVENs` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `plain reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `plain reader` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `no section GIVEN` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 4
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `no section GIVEN` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `as a HENCE` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 6
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `as a HENCE` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 9
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `as a LEST, met` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `as a LEST, missed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 12
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `as a LEST, missed` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 17
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `in a HENCE` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 6
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30

#TRACE `in a HENCE` AT 0 WITH
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 3
  PARTY Alice DOES pay 1 AT 9
  PARTY Bob DOES deliver AT 7
  WAITUNTIL 30
